Notebook[{
 Cell["Levi-Civita, BMPV orientation, and coordinate-density convention", "Title"],
 Cell["A self-contained executable certificate anchored to arXiv:2603.18180 Eq. (4.1) and arXiv:2606.31987 Eqs. (3.7)--(3.8)", "Subtitle"],
 Cell["Purpose. This notebook separates the flat-index Levi-Civita symbol, the curved Levi-Civita tensor (including its vielbein determinant), the BMPV base orientation, the orientation-reversing coordinate chart, and Mathematica's alternating coordinate density.", "Text"],
 Cell["1. Source and BMPV anchors", "Section"],
 Cell["The physical potential is A^I=+H_I^(-1) Theta. The BMPV base orientation is vol4=(r^3/8) Sin[theta] dr wedge dtheta wedge dpsi wedge dphi=-(r^3/8) dr wedge sigma1 wedge sigma2 wedge sigma3. With omega=+j sigma3/(2r^2), d omega is anti-self-dual in this orientation.", "Text"],
 Cell[BoxData["coords={t,r,theta,phi,psi};\narrayIndices={1,2,3,4,5};\nsourceStaticGaugeSign=+1;\nbaseOrientationRelativeToCoordinate=-1;\nchartOrientationRelativeToPhysical=-1;\nsourceAnchorCheck=TrueQ[sourceStaticGaugeSign==1&&baseOrientationRelativeToCoordinate==-1&&chartOrientationRelativeToPhysical==-1];\n<|\"Coordinates\"->coords,\"Eq4.1GaugeSign\"->sourceStaticGaugeSign,\"BaseOrientationRelativeToDrSigma123\"->baseOrientationRelativeToCoordinate,\"ChartOrientationRelativeToPhysical\"->chartOrientationRelativeToPhysical,\"Pass\"->sourceAnchorCheck|>"], "Input"],

 Cell["2. Flat symbol and curved tensor components", "Section"],
 Cell["The ordered flat-index symbol in the orthonormal frame has epsilonLower[0,1,2,3,4]=+1 and epsilonUpper[0,1,2,3,4]=-1. The curved tensor is obtained by transforming with five vielbeins and therefore carries the determinant factor. The vielbein below swaps its last two spatial legs so that it is oriented as the BMPV base while the coordinate order remains (t,r,theta,phi,psi).", "Text"],
 Cell[BoxData["scaleFactors={n0,n1,n2,n3,n4};\nassumptions=And@@Thread[scaleFactors>0];\neta=DiagonalMatrix[{-1,1,1,1,1}];\nvielbein={{n0,0,0,0,0},{0,n1,0,0,0},{0,0,n2,0,0},{0,0,0,0,n4},{0,0,0,n3,0}};\ngMetric=FullSimplify[Transpose[vielbein].eta.vielbein];\ngInverse=Inverse[gMetric];\ndetg=Factor[Det[gMetric]];\ne=Sqrt[-detg];\nalt=Normal[LeviCivitaTensor[5]];\ncoordinateLower=Det[vielbein] alt;\ncoordinateUpper=FullSimplify[(Times@@Diagonal[gInverse]) coordinateLower,assumptions];\nactionAlternatingDensity=alt;\n<|\"Metric\"->gMetric,\"VielbeinDeterminant\"->Factor[Det[vielbein]],\"Determinant\"->detg|>"], "Input"],
 Cell[BoxData["orderedAlt=alt[[Sequence@@arrayIndices]];\nframeLowerOrdered=orderedAlt;\nframeUpperOrdered=(Times@@Diagonal[eta]) frameLowerOrdered;\ncoordinateLowerOrdered=FullSimplify[coordinateLower[[Sequence@@arrayIndices]],assumptions];\ncoordinateUpperOrdered=FullSimplify[coordinateUpper[[Sequence@@arrayIndices]],assumptions];\nframeSignCheck=TrueQ[{frameLowerOrdered,frameUpperOrdered}=={1,-1}];\nvielbeinOrientationCheck=TrueQ[FullSimplify[Det[vielbein]==-e,assumptions]];\ncoordinateSignCheck=TrueQ[FullSimplify[{coordinateLowerOrdered,coordinateUpperOrdered}=={-e,1/e},assumptions]];\nraisingCheck=TrueQ[FullSimplify[(Times@@Diagonal[gInverse]) coordinateLowerOrdered==coordinateUpperOrdered,assumptions]];\nactionArrayCheck=TrueQ[FullSimplify[actionAlternatingDensity==e coordinateUpper,assumptions]];\n<|\"FlatSymbolLower01234\"->frameLowerOrdered,\"FlatSymbolUpper01234\"->frameUpperOrdered,\"CurvedCoordinateLower\"->coordinateLowerOrdered,\"CurvedCoordinateUpper\"->coordinateUpperOrdered,\"VielbeinOrientation\"->vielbeinOrientationCheck,\"RaisingAllIndices\"->raisingCheck,\"AlternatingDensityEqualsSqrtMinusgTimesCurvedUpper\"->actionArrayCheck,\"Pass\"->And[frameSignCheck,vielbeinOrientationCheck,coordinateSignCheck,raisingCheck,actionArrayCheck]|>"], "Input"],

 Cell["3. Component action versus oriented forms", "Section"],
 Cell["A top-form integrated through an orientation-reversing chart acquires one minus sign. Therefore the source's positive coordinate AFF density is the oriented form -A3 wedge F1 wedge F2. Likewise the density e L contains +(lambda/2) epsilonTilde R R A, where epsilonTilde is the alternating coordinate density; equivalently the scalar L contains +(lambda/(2 e)) epsilonTilde R R A. This is the oriented form +2 lambda A wedge tr(R wedge R), with tr(R wedge R)=R^a_b wedge R^b_a=-R^(ab) wedge R_(ab).", "Text"],
 Cell[BoxData["chartSign=-1;\naffOrientedFormCoefficient=-1;\naffAlgebraicCoordinateCoefficient=affOrientedFormCoefficient/4;\naffEffectiveCoordinateDensity=chartSign affAlgebraicCoordinateCoefficient;\naffCheck=TrueQ[affEffectiveCoordinateDensity==1/4];\naWedgeTraceAlgebraicCoefficient=-1/4;\nmixedOrientedFormCoefficient=+2;\nmixedAlgebraicCoordinateCoefficient=mixedOrientedFormCoefficient aWedgeTraceAlgebraicCoefficient;\nmixedEffectiveCoordinateDensity=chartSign mixedAlgebraicCoordinateCoefficient;\nmixedCheck=TrueQ[mixedEffectiveCoordinateDensity==1/2];\n<|\"OrientedAFFCoefficient\"->affOrientedFormCoefficient,\"EffectiveCoordinateAFFCoefficient\"->affEffectiveCoordinateDensity,\"OrientedMixedCoefficient\"->mixedOrientedFormCoefficient,\"EffectiveCoordinateMixedCoefficient\"->mixedEffectiveCoordinateDensity,\"Pass\"->And[affCheck,mixedCheck]|>"], "Input"],

 Cell["4. Maxwell equation and exact rotating BMPV test", "Section"],
 Cell["On the equal-charge locus, the oriented gauge action is -3/2 F wedge star F-A wedge F wedge F. Its variation is proportional to -3[d(star F)+F wedge F]. The Hodge star below uses the curved lower coordinate tensor epsilonLower=-Sqrt[-g] epsilonTilde.", "Text"],
 Cell[BoxData["kineticFormCoefficient=-3/2;\ncubicFormCoefficient=-1;\nkineticVariationCoefficient=2 kineticFormCoefficient;\ncubicVariationCoefficient=3 cubicFormCoefficient;\nvariationCheck=TrueQ[{kineticVariationCoefficient,cubicVariationCoefficient}=={-3,-3}];\nmaxwellEquationLabel=\"d(star F)+F wedge F=0\";\n<|\"VariationCoefficients\"->{kineticVariationCoefficient,cubicVariationCoefficient},\"MaxwellEquation\"->maxwellEquationLabel,\"Pass\"->variationCheck|>"], "Input"],

 Cell[BoxData["h=1+q/r^2;\nomega=j/(2 r^2);\nsigma3={0,0,0,Cos[theta],1};\nthetaOneForm={1,0,0,omega Cos[theta],omega};\nbaseMetric=ConstantArray[0,{5,5}];\nbaseMetric[[2,2]]=h;\nbaseMetric[[3,3]]=h r^2/4;\nbaseMetric[[4,4]]=h r^2/4;\nbaseMetric[[5,5]]=h r^2/4;\nbaseMetric[[4,5]]=h r^2 Cos[theta]/4;\nbaseMetric[[5,4]]=baseMetric[[4,5]];\ngBMPV=FullSimplify[baseMetric-h^-2 Outer[Times,thetaOneForm,thetaOneForm]];\naPlus=FullSimplify[thetaOneForm/h];\nstaticGaugeAnchorCheck=TrueQ[FullSimplify[(aPlus/.j->0)=={1/h,0,0,0,0}]];\nfCov=Table[FullSimplify[D[aPlus[[nu]],coords[[mu]]]-D[aPlus[[mu]],coords[[nu]]]],{mu,5},{nu,5}];\nbmpvAssumptions=q>0&&r>0&&j^2<q^3&&0<theta<Pi;\ndetBMPV=FullSimplify[Det[gBMPV],bmpvAssumptions];\nsqrtgBMPV=r^3 h Sin[theta]/8;\ndeterminantCheck=TrueQ[FullSimplify[sqrtgBMPV^2==-detBMPV,bmpvAssumptions]];\ngBMPVInverse=FullSimplify[Inverse[gBMPV],bmpvAssumptions];\nfRaised=FullSimplify[gBMPVInverse.fCov.Transpose[gBMPVInverse],bmpvAssumptions];\nstarFComponent[a_,b_,c_]:=starFComponent[a,b,c]=FullSimplify[-(sqrtgBMPV/2) Sum[alt[[a,b,c,m,n]] fRaised[[m,n]],{m,5},{n,5}],bmpvAssumptions];\ndStarOn[{a_,b_,c_,d_}]:=FullSimplify[D[starFComponent[b,c,d],coords[[a]]]-D[starFComponent[a,c,d],coords[[b]]]+D[starFComponent[a,b,d],coords[[c]]]-D[starFComponent[a,b,c],coords[[d]]],bmpvAssumptions];\nwedgeFFOn[{a_,b_,c_,d_}]:=FullSimplify[2(fCov[[a,b]]fCov[[c,d]]-fCov[[a,c]]fCov[[b,d]]+fCov[[a,d]]fCov[[b,c]]),bmpvAssumptions];\nfourIndexSets=Subsets[Range[5],{4}];\ndStarValues=dStarOn/@fourIndexSets;\nwedgeFFValues=wedgeFFOn/@fourIndexSets;\nmaxwellResiduals=FullSimplify[dStarValues+wedgeFFValues,bmpvAssumptions];\nmaxwellBackgroundCheck=TrueQ[maxwellResiduals==ConstantArray[0,Length[fourIndexSets]]];\n<|\"StaticAEqualsPlusHInverseDt\"->staticGaugeAnchorCheck,\"MetricDeterminantCheck\"->determinantCheck,\"IndependentFourFormIndices\"->fourIndexSets,\"dStarF\"->dStarValues,\"FwedgeF\"->wedgeFFValues,\"Residuals\"->maxwellResiduals,\"PlusGaugePotentialSolvesMaxwell\"->maxwellBackgroundCheck|>"], "Input"],

 Cell["5. Page and Tachikawa orientation ledger", "Section"],
 Cell["The Maxwell equation makes a star F+C A wedge F closed. The physical induced horizon orientation is -sigma1 wedge sigma2 wedge sigma3. Hence Integral_phys[sigma3 wedge d sigma3]=+16 Pi^2, although the positive coordinate measure gives -16 Pi^2. The physical Tachikawa prefactor is +lambda/G5; the equivalent coordinate-measure implementation has a minus prefactor.", "Text"],
 Cell[BoxData["pageRelativeSign=+1;\npageClosureCheck=TrueQ[pageRelativeSign==1];\nhopfCoordinateIntegral=-16Pi^2;\nhopfPhysicalIntegral=chartSign hopfCoordinateIntegral;\nphysicalTachikawaSign=+1;\ncoordinateTachikawaSign=chartSign physicalTachikawaSign;\nhopfCheck=TrueQ[{hopfPhysicalIntegral,hopfCoordinateIntegral}=={16Pi^2,-16Pi^2}];\ntachikawaCheck=TrueQ[{physicalTachikawaSign,coordinateTachikawaSign}=={1,-1}];\nnumericalProductCheck=TrueQ[physicalTachikawaSign hopfPhysicalIntegral==coordinateTachikawaSign hopfCoordinateIntegral];\n<|\"ClosedPageForm\"->\"a star F+C A wedge F\",\"PhysicalHopfIntegral\"->hopfPhysicalIntegral,\"CoordinateHopfIntegral\"->hopfCoordinateIntegral,\"PhysicalTachikawaSign\"->physicalTachikawaSign,\"CoordinateTachikawaSign\"->coordinateTachikawaSign,\"NumericalProductsAgree\"->numericalProductCheck,\"Pass\"->And[pageClosureCheck,hopfCheck,tachikawaCheck,numericalProductCheck]|>"], "Input"],

 Cell["6. Gauge-variable dictionary and final ledger", "Section"],
 Cell["No field redefinition A to -A is made. The adapted angular variable is beta_I=delta v_I-H_I^(-1) delta omega-omega_0 delta u_I.", "Text"],
 Cell[BoxData["hInv=1/h;\ntimeComponent=hInv+lambda deltaU;\nangularComponent=omega0 hInv+lambda deltaV;\nomegaCorrected=omega0+lambda deltaOmega;\nbeta=Expand[Coefficient[angularComponent-timeComponent omegaCorrected,lambda]];\nbetaCheck=TrueQ[beta==deltaV-hInv deltaOmega-omega0 deltaU];\nsameSignDictionary=<|\"A physical\"->aArchived,\"F physical\"->fArchived,\"delta u physical\"->duArchived,\"delta v physical\"->dvArchived,\"beta physical\"->betaArchived|>;\nsameSignCheck=TrueQ[Values[sameSignDictionary]=={aArchived,fArchived,duArchived,dvArchived,betaArchived}];\n<|\"BetaDefinition\"->beta,\"BetaPass\"->betaCheck,\"SameSignDictionary\"->sameSignDictionary,\"SameSignPass\"->sameSignCheck|>"], "Input"],
 Cell[BoxData["checks=<|\"SourceAndBMPVAnchors\"->sourceAnchorCheck,\"FrameSigns\"->frameSignCheck,\"VielbeinOrientation\"->vielbeinOrientationCheck,\"CoordinateSigns\"->coordinateSignCheck,\"MetricRaising\"->raisingCheck,\"AlternatingArrayDictionary\"->actionArrayCheck,\"AFFFormConversion\"->affCheck,\"MixedFormConversion\"->mixedCheck,\"MaxwellVariation\"->variationCheck,\"StaticGaugeAnchor\"->staticGaugeAnchorCheck,\"BMPVMetricDeterminant\"->determinantCheck,\"ExactRotatingMaxwell\"->maxwellBackgroundCheck,\"PageSign\"->pageClosureCheck,\"HopfOrientation\"->hopfCheck,\"TachikawaOrientation\"->tachikawaCheck,\"TachikawaNumericalEquivalence\"->numericalProductCheck,\"BetaDefinition\"->betaCheck,\"GaugeSigns\"->sameSignCheck|>;\nFinalPass=TrueQ[And@@Values[checks]];\n<|\"Checks\"->checks,\"FinalPass\"->FinalPass|>"], "Input"],
 Cell["Expected final result: every named check and FinalPass are True. This certifies the flat-symbol convention epsilonLower=+1, epsilonUpper=-1; the five-vielbein determinant relation for the curved tensor; the orientation-reversing notebook chart; the archived positive alternating density; the positive Eq. (4.1) gauge potential; and the physical Page and Tachikawa signs.", "Text"]
}, WindowTitle->"Levi-Civita and BMPV orientation certificate", StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb"]
